# Notices some crates keep beside their license texts, in files
# cargo-about does not read: copyright lines of code they took from
# others, or of their own authors where the license text has none.
# scripts/notices.sh copies each file, from the crate's own source as
# cargo resolves it, into THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES after the crates'
# licenses. One line a crate version. For a crate named here, the
# script fails if a version of it is built that has no line, if a line
# names a version no longer built or a crate no longer in the tree, or
# if a file's sha256 is not the one here: a bump of a listed crate
# stops the build until the new file is read and its line updated.
# It cannot see a crate that is not named here: deleting all of a
# crate's lines drops its notice without a word, and a crate newly in
# the tree that keeps such a file is found only by reading it.
